	keywords = {Benchmarking; Chains; Computation theory; Computer vision; Diagnosis; Error detection; Forestry; Health risks; Hierarchical systems; Query languages; Query processing; Reliability analysis; Reliability theory; Risk analysis; Risk assessment; Safety engineering; System theory; Transparency; Uncertainty analysis; Visual languages; Actionable error attribution; Adversarial robustness; Causal attributions; Causal reasoning; Causal reasoning capability; Compositional complexity; Comprehensive hallucination evaluation; Cross-domain evaluations; Cross-modal; Cross-modal inconsistency; Domain specific; Domain-specific benchmark; Domain-specific query; Dynamic knowledge; Evidence chains; Evidence grounding; Evolving benchmark; Factuality assessment; Faithfulness evaluation; Generative AI evaluation; Ground truth; Ground truth ambiguity; Hallucination evaluation; Hallucination mitigation; Hierarchical queries; Hierarchical query decomposition; Horizontal vs vertical evaluation; Interpretability; Language model; Large language model; LENS framework; Mechanistic interpretability; Mechanistics; Metacognitive evaluation; Metacognitives; Multi dimensional; Multi-dimensional metric; Multi-layered; Multi-layered assessment structure; Multi-modal; Multimodal hallucination; Post-hoc error detection; Proactive risk assessment; Query decomposition; Reasoning capabilities; Reasoning failure; Reliability and robustness; Retrieval-augmented generation; Risks assessments; Selection accuracy; Surface-level accuracy; Temporal drifts; Tool necessity detection; Tool selection; Tool selection accuracy; Traceable evidence chain; Transparency and interpretability; Tree-of-thought; Trustworthy AI; Uncertainty quantifications; Universal village; User-centric; User-centric benchmark construction; Vision-language model; Visual-textual misalignment; Computational efficiency},
